The Police and Border Guard Board (PPA) has stepped up its border checks, and not only at the eastern border, but also in Valga, on the Latvian border.
As 41 people who had entered Estonia illegally across the Latvian border were apprehended over the past week, authorities are increasingly checking people and vehicles arriving from Latvia at the border.
The checks were boosted more than usual in Valga on Monday when "Aktuaalne kaamera visited".
"This is migration pressure that may have been initiated by the Belarusian state, but if we are talking about the countries of origin of these migrants, we have apprehended Somali citizens as the largest number, followed by people from other East African countries, including Ethiopia, as well as more distant countries such as India, Pakistan and Bangladesh. There are actually many countries of origin," said Igor…
